From: Lars Slettan Øydneskleiv <larsoyd@github.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 02:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: Treat IFileSaveDialog cosmetic property stubs as
 non-fatal.

IFileSaveDialog::SetCollectedProperties() and IFileSaveDialog::SetSaveAsItem()
were both complete E_NOTIMPL stubs. Both are cosmetic/UI-hint methods on real
Windows: SetCollectedProperties only affects what property columns the Vista
Explorer-style Save dialog's optional properties panel shows, and SetSaveAsItem
only supplies a preferred initial entry for that same dialog (the dialog's
actual save target is still driven by SetFileName/SetFolder, which Wine already
implements). Neither is documented to affect whether the save operation itself
succeeds.

An application that calls either of these while building an IFileSaveDialog
and checks SUCCEEDED() before continuing (a completely reasonable assumption
given real Windows never fails either call for ordinary arguments) never
reaches IFileDialog::Show() at all under Wine — the save dialog silently never
appears, with no error surfaced to the user.

Found via Windows Movie Maker 6.0: File > Save produced no visible dialog
window. Live winedbg tracing plus raw disassembly of MOVIEMK.dll's internal
ComGetSaveFileName helper (which drives the whole IFileSaveDialog setup
sequence: SetFileTypes, SetOptions, SetCollectedProperties, SetTitle,
SetDefaultExtension, SetSaveAsItem, ..., Show) showed each step gated by an
explicit SUCCEEDED()-style check that jumps straight to a common failure-return
path on FAILED(hr), with SetCollectedProperties(NULL, FALSE) — the exact
arguments observed live — being the first of two such checks to trip on Wine's
E_NOTIMPL stubs; SetSaveAsItem would have been the second, later in the same
chain, had the first not already aborted it.

This treats both methods the same way IFileDialog2_fnAddPlace (an adjacent,
already-non-fatal cosmetic stub in the same vtable family) is already treated:
keep the FIXME so the gap stays visible in traces, but return S_OK instead of
E_NOTIMPL so callers that reasonably assume Windows-correct behavior aren't
blocked by a UI feature Wine's dialog (native or XDG-portal-backed) doesn't
need in order to complete a save.

Confirmed via a minimal winegcc harness driving the real comdlg32.dll
(CoCreateInstance(CLSID_FileSaveDialog) + the exact SetCollectedProperties/
SetSaveAsItem argument shapes observed live): both calls return E_NOTIMPL
before this patch, S_OK after. Confirmed against the real application: File >
Save now reaches and displays the Save dialog, and a project saved through it
is written to disk and registered in the shell's Recent Items
(IPersistFile_fnSaveCompleted fires with the real target path), where
previously the dialog never appeared at all.
---
 dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
index ed51e3028b0..40618aa30ef 100644
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/itemdlg.c
@@ -4127,7 +4127,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IFileSaveDialog_fnSetSaveAsItem(IFileSaveDialog* iface, IS
 {
     FileDialogImpl *This = impl_from_IFileSaveDialog(iface);
     FIXME("stub - %p (%p)\n", This, psi);
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    return S_OK;
 }

 static HRESULT WINAPI IFileSaveDialog_fnSetCollectedProperties(IFileSaveDialog* iface,
@@ -4143,7 +4143,7 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IFileSaveDialog_fnSetCollectedProperties(IFileSaveDialog*
 {
     FileDialogImpl *This = impl_from_IFileSaveDialog(iface);
     FIXME("stub - %p (%p, %d)\n", This, pList, fAppendDefault);
-    return E_NOTIMPL;
+    return S_OK;
 }

 static HRESULT WINAPI IFileSaveDialog_fnGetProperties(IFileSaveDialog* iface, IPropertyStore **ppStore)
--
2.45.2
